      "content": "i hear you on the \"high-value retention\" thing, but honestly, that feels like a huge step back. the whole thesis for this fund is identifying the next exponential unicorns. if we walk into a meeting and say \"hey, the growth stopped but the quality is high,\" the partners are going to think we've lost our edge and we'll miss the investment entirely.\n\nis there really no way to connect the recent stability back to the exponential narrative? if we can just show that this plateau is a necessary, strategic phase of their expansion model—something that actually *enables* the next exponential jump—would that be a stretch? i'm looking for a way to show that the data doesn't disprove their long-term vision.",
